==Battleground==
*4 [[Gudetama Plate (Enemy)|Gudetama Plates]] (1,000%) spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Gudetama Plate (Enemy)|Gudetama Plate]] (10%) spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Gudegude à la mode (Enemy)|Gudegude à la modes]] spawn, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
**1 [[Nisetama Army (Enemy)|Nisetama Army]] spawns.
**Infinite [[Gudetama Plate (Enemy)|Gudetama Plates]] (1,000%) spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**3 [[Gudebene Cat (Enemy)|Gudebene Cats]] spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The Gudetama Plates are Single Attack, you can take advantage of that and spam multiple [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho Cats]] to hold them off while you build up backliners like [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Crimson Mina]] and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]]. Once the Gudetama Plates die, you start spamming [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs]] Cat alongside [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]]  to deal good damage. The enemies will push without enough meatshields, so include at least two others in the form of [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] as well as [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]]. In truth, the boss wave won't really pose too much of a problem as long as you're meatshielding properly.

